Grocery Store Project — Code Change Reference

If the lecturer says…

Change this

Change the colours/theme

frontend/src/index.css → :root block (--header-green, --forest-900, --warm-500, etc.)

Rename or add a menu link

src/config/siteConfig.js → NAV_LINKS

Change contact info/footer

siteConfig.js → CONTACT_INFO; layout in Footer.jsx

Change the logo

src/assets/logo/ and BrandLogo.jsx

Change free-shipping amount or fee

Update both siteConfig.js → SHIPPING_INFO (display) and backend/config/shipping.js → FREE_SHIPPING_ABOVE (actual calculation)

Add a sort option

ProductsPage.jsx → SORTERS and the options list near lines 16–26

Add a filter

ShopFilters.jsx → filter UI; ProductsPage.jsx → filtered block for filter logic

Change button or label text

Search the text in the source code; also check src/i18n/translations.js

Add a field to products (e.g., type or weight)

1. backend/models/Product.js 2. Product create/update routes 3. AdminProductForm.jsx 4. ProductCard.jsx or ProductDetailPage.jsx

Add an order status

backend/models/Order.js, AdminOrderDetail.jsx, and lib/orderFormat.js

Add a user role

ROLES in backend/routes/adminUserRoutes.js, the User model, and AdminUser.jsx

Change a password or form rule

Backend validation in authRoutes.js and the form in Register.jsx

Change the quantity limit in the cart

QuantityControl.jsx and updateQuantity in StoreContext.jsx

Important reminders

Check the existing code before editing because file paths and line numbers may change.

For shipping changes, update both the displayed settings and the backend calculation.

For new product fields, verify that the field is saved, updated, validated, and displayed correctly.

For new order statuses or user roles, check both backend rules and frontend UI.

After changes, test the affected feature and run the project to check for errors.

Note: File paths and identifiers above are based on the project's current reference notes. Verify them against the actual source code before making changes.